  "findings": {
    "single_query_depth2_ladybug": "Not adopted. LadybugDB 0.21.2, 100k edges: (1) a two-hop pattern (s {node_id:$x})-[e1]-(m)-[e2]-(o) with any predicate on e1 returns wrong results (world seed 11: 33 middle nodes one hop, 25 in the two-hop pattern; pinning a missing middle node returns all its rows); (2) any MATCH after a WITH, from an UNWIND or from computed ids is planned as a full relationship scan: 50-55 ms (anchored on a parameter: 3-5 ms); pipeline variants measured 64-150 ms; (3) in-query collect/list_sort per group costs 3x the plain rows; path property extraction from a recursive rel 40-136 ms. So depth 1 is one query and depth 2 is two filtered queries (one per level).",
    "engine_search_bottleneck_ladybug": "Engine.search p95 50.3 ms (empty-graph baseline 9.8): the read leg's 6-seed frontier_edges fetch is an IN-anchored two-part union (~22 ms; IN costs a node-table scan in LadybugDB); RM-96 cut it from ~25-36 ms by deduplicating in Python instead of a NOT IN predicate. The run-to-run noise on this host is about +-5 ms (run 1 measured 66.6 ms before the dedupe change, the RM-115 run 48.1 ms).",
    "single_query_neo4j": "Adopted: one qualified_walk Cypher query per walk (depth 1 and 2): level 1 per seed, ordered collect sliced to max_degree; level 2 the 16 strongest level-1 nodes, each sliced to the deep degree; node rows and (subgraph) induced edges in CALL subqueries. Needs an index on the node id property (created once per store before the first pushed-down walk or frontier_edges call): without it each per-row id lookup scanned the label (p95 669 ms depth 1, 1388 ms depth 2)."
